formatted_question:
According to the paper "Controlling Text-to-Image Diffusion by Orthogonal Finetuning", how can OFT's forward pass be rewritten in terms of the pretrained weight matrix $\bm{W}^0$ and the orthogonal transform $\bm{R}$?
(A) \bm{z}=(\bm{R}\bm{W}^0)^\top\bm{x}=(\bm{W}^0+(\bm{R}-\bm{I})\bm{W}^0)^\top\bm{x}
(B) \bm{z}=(\bm{W}^0\bm{R})^\top\bm{x}=(\bm{W}^0+\bm{W}^0(\bm{R}-\bm{I}))^\top\bm{x}
(C) \bm{z}=(\bm{W}^0+\bm{B}\bm{A})^\top\bm{x}
(D) \bm{z}=(\bm{R}\bm{W}^0)^\top\bm{x}=(\bm{W}^0+\bm{R}-\bm{I})^\top\bm{x}
(E) \bm{z}=(\bm{R}^\top\bm{W}^0)^\top\bm{x}=(\bm{W}^0+(\bm{R}^\top-\bm{I})\bm{W}^0)^\top\bm{x}

